File Index

/audited.ts
Purpose: The public layer carries LESS than the audited file, on purpose: room history (merge before-images) and every `player` record in a baseline's `contents` and `was` are dropped, so nothing about a person can reach the site. Each slice is a valid map file alone: links are written into the slice of the area their exit starts in, and `offPage` is RECOMPUTED from where the target is (another area, or none), never trusted from the input. The strict reader runs on the input and on every slice before anything is returned, so a bad slice (for example a merged room whose surviving room is in another area) stops the whole publish. File names are narrower than ids: an area id with `.`, `_` or `:` is valid in the map but cannot be a file name here (the C# reader accepts only lower-case slugs), so it is refused by name. Pure: the caller gzips, hashes (`versionId`) and writes (scripts/publish-audited.mjs); the manifest it returns has no `versionId` or `bytes` yet. Change together with Server.Dsl/AgentApi/WorldMapApi.cs in the DSL repo, which reads this manifest and these slices.
